> ## D1.4 Intent worker [r2: fencing, fairness, classification]
89,113c118,160
< - Application service `MessageAdmissions` (port `MessageIntentQueue`: claim/finish/defer with
<   lease fencing; port reads on bindings; `WorkflowService::admit`; `WorkflowWaits` reply delivery).
<   Claim: `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`, oldest `available_at`, at most 4 per company per page (window
<   function), page ≤ 32, lease 60 s; claim increments `attempts`; lease expiry consumes the attempt;
<   `attempts = 5` → `failed` (observable, not reclaimed). Poison-batch regression test required.
< - Processing one intent, in order:
<   1. **Reply correlation (D1.5).** If matched → outcome `matched(run)`, done; no admission.
<   2. **Eligible bindings:** active bindings with a non-NULL `message_trigger`, association
<      `Channel(channel_id)` or `Thread(channel_id, thread_id)`, whose rule admits the facts
<      (`replies_to_workflow` derived from `reply_to_message_id` here). Evaluated at processing time
<      against current activation: deactivation before processing stops admission ("disabling a
<      binding stops future admissions"); this is documented, not hidden.
<   3. For each eligible binding without an outcome row: `admit` with actor = run-as,
<      association `Thread{channel, thread}`, trigger `Message{message_id}` with
<      `trigger_id = intent.id`, idempotency key `m:{intent}:{binding}`, correlation = the message's,
<      input = `MessageTriggerInput` built from the stored canonical message (identifiers only in
<      the intent; content read at admission), delivery policy from the intent (D1.7). Result:
<      `Created|Replayed` → `admitted(run)`; deterministic refusal (`NotFound`, `BadRequest`,
<      `Conflict`, authorization) → `refused(code)`; transient error → stop, defer the intent
<      (backoff), later attempts skip bindings that already have outcome rows.
<   4. Done when every eligible binding has an outcome; intent outcome `admitted` or `none`.
< - Each binding is admitted independently: one refusal never blocks a sibling binding. Admission's
<   `(company, binding, source_key)` uniqueness keeps "one run per binding per message" even across
<   intent retries, duplicate workers, or a crash between admission commit and outcome write.
< - Wake: in-process `Notify` after an inbound commit that created intents, plus a 1 s poll.
---
> 1. **Claim (F008):** a CTE ranks available `pending` rows (and `claimed` rows whose lease expired)
>    per company by `available_at` without locking, keeps ≤4 per company, orders by `available_at`,
>    limits the page to 32, then `SELECT … FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED` on those ids and sets
>    `claimed`, `worker_id`, a fresh `claim_generation`, `lease_expires_at = now()+60s`, and
>    `attempts+1`. A row reaching attempt 5 whose lease expires (or that is deferred at 5) goes to
>    `failed` (never reclaimed). Every write after the claim — finish, defer, and **each per-binding
>    outcome row** — requires `(id, worker_id, claim_generation)` and an unexpired lease in the same
>    statement; a stale worker's write affects zero rows and it stops. Poison-batch and tenant-burst
>    tests (company A with 100 pending, company B with 1 → B in the first page).
> 2. **Reply correlation (D1.5)** first. `Matched` → outcome `matched(run)`, done. `NotYet` → defer
>    (D1.5.3). `Unmatched` → continue.
> 3. If `admissible` is false → outcome `none`, done (a quiet message never admits).
> 4. **Eligible bindings:** active, `activated_at <= intent.created_at`, non-NULL `message_trigger`,
>    association `Channel(channel_id)` or `Thread(channel_id, thread_id)`, rule admits the facts.
>    Read with each binding's current configuration revision.
> 5. For each eligible binding without an outcome row, `admit` with actor = that revision's run-as,
>    association `Thread{channel, thread}`, trigger `Message{message_id}` (`trigger_id = intent.id`),
>    idempotency key `m:{intent}:{binding}`, **expected binding revision** = the evaluated revision
>    (new optional `AdmitWorkflowRequest.binding_revision`), the message's correlation id, input
>    `MessageTriggerInput` built from the stored message, delivery policy from the intent.
>    **Classification (F005), by producing condition:**
>    - `Created|Replayed(run)` → `admitted(run)`.
>    - **`Stale`** (new `AdmissionResult` variant: the binding's current configuration revision or
>      selection differs from the expected/pre-read one — the condition `verify_current` reports as
>      `Conflict` today) → re-read the binding and re-evaluate eligibility, at most 3 times in this
>      attempt; ineligible after re-read → no outcome row (the binding no longer wants it);
>      still stale after 3 → treated as transient.
>    - Binding inactive/archived/missing, run-as not owner/admin or not visible, resources not
>      ready, input rejected by the schema (`NotFound`, `Forbidden`, `BadRequest` from the admission
>      preflight/verification) → `refused(code)`.
>    - `AdmissionResult::Conflict` (same key, different input/association — a key-derivation bug)
>      → `failed(key_conflict)`, logged as an error.
>    - Anything else (`Database`, timeouts, `Internal`) → transient for **this binding only**:
>      record nothing, continue with sibling bindings, then defer the intent with backoff. On the
>      final attempt, bindings still without an outcome get `failed(transient_exhausted)`.
> 6. **Refusal visibility (F006, P08-Q2):** each `refused`/`failed` row emits a structured warning
>    (company, binding, intent, reason) and increments `workflow_message_admission_refusals_total
>    {reason}`; B3's binding read route returns the latest refusal per binding and a refusal count;
>    B4 projects bindings with recent refusals into the attention list.
> 7. Done when every eligible binding has an outcome (or is no longer eligible): outcome `admitted`
>    if any admitted, else `none`. Each binding is admitted independently; `(company, binding,
>    source_key)` uniqueness keeps one run per (binding, message) across retries and workers.
> 8. Wake: in-process `Notify` after a commit that created intents, plus a 1 s poll.
