> 1. **Reserved event.** Name `message.reply`. Correlation = the outbound canonical message id the
>    reply answers. Authors write `wait.event: {event: {literal: message.reply}, correlation:
>    {ref: /steps/<S>/output/messages/<n>/message_id}}` (`message_result` already lists
>    `messages[i].message_id`). **[r2] Registry-fixed payload (F004.3):** a `wait.event` whose literal
>    event is `message.reply` must declare exactly the registry's `MessageTriggerInput` schema as its
>    payload schema (or omit it and receive it); publication refuses anything else.
> 2. **Candidate.** `reply_to_message_id` equals a `workflow_message_destinations.message_id` whose
>    `thread_id` is the intent's thread → `(run, destination, publishing step S)`: S is the step of
>    the publishing execution (`workflow_message_actions.execution_id` → `workflow_executions`)
>    when `origin = 'step'`. A `model_tool` publication (an agent tool's send) has no step output a
>    wait can reference, so it is never awaited. No candidate → `Unmatched`.
> 3. **Matched only for an awaited correlation (F002).** The run's frozen graph must contain a
>    `message.reply` wait step W whose `correlation` binding is a reference into `/steps/S/…`;
>    none → `Unmatched` (reply to an unawaited send). Otherwise look at W's waits for this
>    correlation:
>    - an open (`waiting`) wait with `event_name='message.reply'` and this correlation → deliver;
>    - a settled/expired/cancelled/failed one and no open one → `Unmatched` (wait over: ordinary
>      ingress);
>    - none yet and the run is live → `NotYet`: defer the intent (event-before-park) until W parks,
>      the run ends, or `REPLY_PARK_GRACE = 5 min` after acceptance, after which → `Unmatched`.
>    The run not live → `Unmatched`.
> 4. **Responder identity (F003).** The intent's `responder_principal_id` must equal the
>    destination's expected responder: `user` → `principal_id`; `reply` → the source message's
>    author principal; `channel` → intent `origin = 'application'` (an in-app reply posted by a
>    member through the UI, which authorizes channel access) with a non-NULL responder principal. Mismatch → `Unmatched` (the intended
>    recipient's real answer can still match later). **User-send participation:** publishing a
>    `user` destination records the member's principal as a `Participant` of the new thread it opens
>    (`thread_principals`, same transaction), so the member's email reply passes thread injection
>    as a party of that dedicated thread only; it joins no customer conversation (user sends always
>    open their own thread).
> 5. **Delivery port (F004.1/.2).** `WorkflowWaits::deliver_reply(ReplyEvent{run, wait step W,
>    correlation, event_id = UUIDv5(intent.id), payload})` → under the run's producer advisory lock,
>    in this order: (a) event id exists → `Duplicate` if identical, else `Conflict`; (b) recheck the
>    open wait for (run, W, `message.reply`, correlation) → none → `Unmatched`/`NotYet` as in 3;
>    (c) any unconsumed or consumed `message.reply` event for (run, correlation) already exists →
>    `Unmatched` (one response per wait); (d) `record_event_on`. Outcome mapping in the worker:
>    `Recorded|Duplicate` → matched; `Unmatched` → continue to admission; `NotYet` → defer;
>    `BadRequest` (payload rejected — unreachable with D1.5.1, treated as a bug) → `Unmatched` +
>    error log; `Conflict` (event id reused for different content, or inbox full) → `Unmatched` +
>    error log; `Database`/timeout → transient (defer the intent). Crash-replay: event recorded,
>    outcome not written → retry hits (a) → `Duplicate` → matched, no admission.
